00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.170
With that, let's dive back into this.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.423
Let's talk about the prophet Joseph Smith.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.810
Joseph Smith was born in the perfect place

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.422
at the perfect time.

00:03:20.422 --> 00:03:23.160
It was the early 1800s and
the U.S. had just thrown off

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.200
England to become a new country,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.780
and it was going through
some massive growing pains.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.750
Most of these new Americans who
had just left the old world,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.290
rejected a lot of old world
things, namely religion.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.450
Only 10% of white Americans regularly

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.860
attended church at this time.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.300
So to help revive God,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.790
you have all these super
charismatic preachers who left

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.120
the cities and went out to
the countryside to preach.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.730
And this led to an explosion
of religious thought,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.890
especially in upstate New York.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.440
So now you have all these
like hyper reformist religions

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.610
that were replacing old style,
authoritarian type churches.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.860
All these new wild religious flavors

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.310
that were more emotional,
expressive and personal.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.230
I mean, none of us were
alive at this time,

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:07.230
but you can kind of imagine
like this brand new country

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.000
founded on these new ideals.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.040
It was unprecedented times.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.260
America felt special and different,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.000
but also kind of scary.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.650
Revolution in the new world,

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.130
new science, magical
technology, new ideas,

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.320
both wholesome and sinful,

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.933
all of it speeding up
at an increasing rate.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.930
For a lot of people this was a sign,

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.000
a sign that the end of
the world was coming

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.890
and that Jesus, like he prophesied,

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:35.700
would come back to usher in
this thousand years of glory

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.320
for those who believed in him.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.960
And a thousand years of
fire, for those who didn't.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.700
This was called the Millennium.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:42.840
So a lot of these new churches

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.510
that were cropping up kind
of claimed to be the place

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.910
that was preparing the
earth for the second coming,

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.550
like they were God's chosen
administrators on the earth

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.800
in the final days before it all ended.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.990
It was scary, it was exciting,

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:59.370
and God was talking to
people again in new ways.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:02.160
And this is the context that
Joseph Smith was born into.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.580
In 1805, born to a mother who was swept up

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.500
in the excitement of
all these new religions

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.020
and a father who wasn't
really religious at all.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.670
It was kind of like a lot
of people at the time,

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:15.066
a family that was religiously
lost, but not for long.

00:05:15.066 --> 00:05:17.340
(suspenseful music)

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.920
In addition to being a
frothy religious environment,

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.440
upstate New York was also a place

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.080
where people hunted for treasure.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.080
There was this culture
of folk magic and legends

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.300
that led to the search
for riches and jewels

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.120
that were potentially
buried by Spanish explorers

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.970
or pirates of the past or artifacts

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.883
that were hidden in Native
American burial mounds.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.910
And their methods for
hunting for all this treasure

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:44.160
were mystical and magical.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.550
They used seer stones, crystals, rods,

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.110
visions through dreams,

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.573
all of this to help them
locate buried treasure.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.710
And young Joseph Smith was very caught up

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.660
in this treasure hunting craze.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.210
He wasn't educated, he
barely had any schooling

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.500
he could kind of read and write.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.710
He wasn't religious, but from a young age

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.100
he showed himself as a
skilled treasure hunter.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.540
I mean, let's keep some perspective.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.373
In all of our research,

00:06:10.373 --> 00:06:13.320
we didn't find a single
like document showing

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.790
that he actually found any treasure,

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:18.180
but he managed to convey
to the people around him

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:21.210
that he was an expert treasure hunter,

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.410
using mythical methods.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.510
So this is the context that
you need to know to really

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.500
understand this story.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.540
We're in upstate New
York in the early 1800s.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.230
There is this frenzy of folk
magic and treasure hunting,

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.320
and the place is a blaze
with religious fervor.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.940
And there's talk of the last days

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.740
and the millennium of fire and glory

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.420
that was coming any day now.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.996
But the story really begins
in the spring of 1820.

00:06:42.996 --> 00:06:47.996
(birds chirpy)
(folksy music)

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.530
Joseph, a 14 year old boy
gets curious about religion.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.000
And after visiting a bunch of churches

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.200
and finding no answers,

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:01.710
he decides to go into a
grove of trees to ask God,

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.300
which church was true.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.950
This movie that we're watching right now,

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:08.400
I know by heart because I've
watched it hundreds of times,

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.380
of course, dubbed in Spanish.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.000
I was a missionary in Tijuana,

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:12.930
and the first thing

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.570
that I would teach people was this story.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.640
And I would often show them this movie.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:21.900
- [Joseph Smith] I kneeled
down and began to offer up

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.640
the desires of my heart.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.860
- So Joseph Smith is in this grove

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.120
and he's praying and after
a run in with the devil.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.656
- [Joseph Smith] Exerting all
my strength to call upon God.

00:07:33.656 --> 00:07:35.910
(suspenseful music)

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.043
- He sees a pillar of light,

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.233
brighter than the sun
directly over his head.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.100
And within that light,

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:51.630
he sees two people whose
brightness defy all description.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.340
He finds out that it's God the Father

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.170
and his son, Jesus Christ.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:58.080
And Jesus goes on to tell
him that none of the churches

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.390
that he's been investigating are true

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.510
and that instead Joseph is being called

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:06.810
to do the work of God, to
restore the real true church

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.970
that had been lost from the earth.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.380
To restore this church,

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.680
to prepare the world for
the second coming of Jesus

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.660
and the millennium that he will usher in.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.860
This event is referred
to as the first vision

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.800
and it is the founding
story of the LDS Church,

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.200
The Mormon Church, like
most people know it.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.370
As a member of the church

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:29.160
from a very young age
you learn this story,

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:32.040
you sing about it, you talk
about it, you study it,

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.750
and every few years the church comes out

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.843
with a new video version
representing the first vision.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.040
Okay, so this is just the beginning.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.990
A few years go by, Joseph
doesn't tell anyone

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.990
about his vision, but by 1823,

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.930
Joseph is a late teenager
and one night he's sleeping

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.360
in his like little humble
cabin with his family

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.060
and he says that an angel appears to him.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.860
The angel is named Moroni.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.450
By the way, if you ever
see a Mormon temple,

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.790
big white building, you
will see a depiction

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.070
of the angel Moroni on the top of

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.870
that temple with a trumpet pointing east.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.840
But for now, he's an angel
in Joseph Smith's room

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.510
telling young Joseph that,
yes, the second coming

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:12.300
of Christ is right around
the corner and that yes,

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.280
just like God and Jesus
told him a few years ago,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.800
he has been called to prepare the world

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.940
for the second coming.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.440
And if that wasn't enough,

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.470
Moroni tells him that there
is a book that is written

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.600
on golden plates that is buried

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.850
in a hill near Joseph's house.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.550
The book is an important
record of a group of Jews

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:33.390
who left Jerusalem in 600
BC and came to the Americas.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.017
Anyway, I'll explain that in just a second

00:09:35.017 --> 00:09:37.650
"And don't worry," says
Moroni, "along with the plates,

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:39.690
there's the gear you need to translate

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.550
these plates into English."

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.050
Joseph just needs to get a bit older

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.330
and he'll be ready to
translate the plates.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.090
At this point, Joseph tells his
family what's been happening

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.020
and they believe him.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.960
So by the time he's 21, he's
instructed to go to the hill,

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.690
Cumorah, near his house
and get the plates.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.030
Okay, so now Joseph Smith in his twenties,

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:00.300
he's this uneducated,
unreligious, treasure hunter,

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.840
and he starts to focus in
on something totally new.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.790
In the words of one believing Mormon

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.657
historian Richard Bushman,

00:10:07.657 --> 00:10:10.680
"He starts to orient
himself away from treasure

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.953
and towards translation",
he's becoming a prophet.

00:10:15.919 --> 00:10:19.002
(suspenseful music)

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.920
So Joseph says he goes
and gets these plates

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.270
and people try to rob him,

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.340
but eventually he gets them secured.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.530
And in a little cabin in rural New York,

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:31.950
Joseph begins the work
of translating this stack

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:35.487
of metal plates that no
one else is allowed to see.

00:10:35.487 --> 00:10:38.280
(suspenseful music)

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.740
He would sit on one side of a curtain

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.480
so that no one else could see,

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.940
and he says he looked through these stones

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:48.240
at the Egyptian engravings
on these golden plates,

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.950
and they would turn into English,

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:53.010
and then he would dictate
them out loud to a scribe,

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:55.920
sometimes his wife or other
early believers who were

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.650
supporting him and that
scribe would write them down.

00:10:58.650 --> 00:10:59.483
At other points,

00:10:59.483 --> 00:11:01.290
Joseph didn't even need
the plates to translate.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.910
He could hide them somewhere else

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.920
and he would use his personal seer stone,

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.020
the one that he used back when
he was just a treasure hunter

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.150
before he says he was called as a prophet,

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:11.810
this little chocolate
colored egg shaped stone.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.120
He would put it into a hat and
then he would bury his face

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.300
in the hat and he said that
the stone would light up

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.150
with the word that he was
supposed to dictate to his scribe.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:22.950
His scribe would write it down

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.840
and the Book of Mormon was being written.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.090
Now listen, all of this seems really weird

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:29.400
and wild to us now,
very easily like, okay,

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.690
clearly this guy's making it up,

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.390
but at the time, mystical
visions and treasure hunting

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:36.180
and seer stones, this was
all very normal in society.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.610
Folk magic, native American artifacts,

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:40.020
none of this was very fringe.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.360
And Joseph, Joseph had been doing stuff

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.760
like this for a decade,
which is why his parents

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.790
and other people in his
community supported him.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.200
The difference though at this time is

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.930
that he was blending his
treasure hunting skills

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:56.130
and his folk magic sensibilities
with this religious revival

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:58.290
that was happening at the time to create

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.536
something kind of unique.

00:12:00.536 --> 00:12:02.580
(birds chirping)

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.020
So anyway, he's in his early twenties,

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.640
he's translating the Book of Mormon.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.380
He faces a bunch of ups and downs,

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.540
he goes through a few scribes and after

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.630
a very productive 90
day window, 24 year old,

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:17.130
barely educated Joseph Smith
finishes dictating 588 pages

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.701
of text that would become
the Book of Mormon.

00:12:19.701 --> 00:12:22.830
(birds chirping)

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.950
Joseph says that he gives
the plates back to Moroni

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:29.490
and then takes the manuscript
of the pages to a printer.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:30.750
That's how we have the Book of Mormon.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.050
This is my Book of Mormon.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:38.803
Maps, my early exposure to maps.

00:12:38.803 --> 00:12:39.990
(pages turning)

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.160
So the Book of Mormon is
incredibly important to this story

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:47.580
because it was the main
validator for Joseph Smith

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:50.700
in those early days and continues
to be a foundational part

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.890
for believers in the LDS faith.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.640
That's because Joseph Smith
wasn't religious or educated

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.190
and now suddenly he's
writing this Bible like book

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.330
in a few months.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.520
And yes, this book is
definitely full of a lot

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:06.450
of like full blown copy and
paste jobs from like the Bible.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:10.950
But there's also like a lot
of really compelling stuff in

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:14.730
here in terms of religious
lessons, complex histories,

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.160
nods back to like an understanding

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.530
of Hebrew language and culture.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:24.030
This is not the type of guy
that his town saw him as.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.070
He was a treasure hunter and a farm kid,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.010
not a religious man, and
definitely not a prophet.

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:30.870
- [Speaker 2] Mr. Smith,
could you tell me more

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.520
about that book?

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.650
- Yes, yes, I could.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:36.870
- Okay, so let's be clear
on what Joseph Smith said

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.330
The Book of Mormon is, it's
not what a lot of people say,

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:40.770
which is like the Mormon Bible.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:44.400
The book tells the story of
a group of Jews in Jerusalem

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.900
in around 600 BC.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:47.100
They're told to leave the city

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.330
before it gets destroyed.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.030
So they leave the city, they
walk in the desert for a while,

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.370
probably to like Oman is
what a lot of Mormons think.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.430
And then they build a boat
and travel across the ocean

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:59.430
for a very long time until
they reach the Americas,

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:02.310
somewhere in like North
Central or South America.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.560
The foundation of the story
is about these brothers

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.260
of the original family who
like eventually split off

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.450
and they like hate each
other and they grow up into

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.220
these two different civilizations,

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.470
the Nephites and the Lamanites
who are always fighting

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:14.303
with each other.

00:14:14.303 --> 00:14:15.136
And there's all these prophets

00:14:15.136 --> 00:14:16.920
and there's all this drama that happens.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.920
And the introduction to
my Book of Mormons says,

00:14:21.967 --> 00:14:25.020
"The Lamanites", these people
came over from Jerusalem,

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:29.280
are quote "the principle ancestors
of the American Indians."

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:32.130
And a few years ago they did
change that to, "The Lamanites

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.280
being among the ancestors
of the American Indians."

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.260
But yeah, the point is
that the Book of Mormon

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:41.370
is a history of these Jews
turned indigenous Americans.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:45.060
And unsurprisingly, there's a
whole community of believers

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.980
who work to validate

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:49.560
that this is actually a historic record.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:53.190
But no, in the reality there's
no archeological, genetic,

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:55.740
or linguistic evidence that
supports the Book of Mormon's

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:58.590
assertion that Jewish people migrated

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.440
to the Americas around 600 BC.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.110
For believers, the most
important part of this book

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.820
is the climax of the whole thing,

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:10.020
where in 33 AD Jesus, having
recently been crucified

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.120
over in the old world, in Jerusalem,

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.800
gets resurrected over there

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.130
and comes to visit the people in America,

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:18.840
which is where this painting came from.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.370
This is a painting that is hanging

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.130
in a lot of LDS churches.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:27.960
It shows Jesus Christ among
the ancient civilizations

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.430
of the Americas.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:33.389
Yeah, some pretty wild stories.

00:15:33.389 --> 00:15:35.730
(suspenseful music)

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:36.840
(birds chirping)

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.100
So yeah, I know we're all over the place

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.260
and we'll get back to Joseph
Smith's life for a second.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:44.520
But as someone who has read
this book dozens of times,

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.250
I can tell you that
when you're a believer,

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.560
this is a really compelling piece of work.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:52.170
You can read these pages and
you can read about the stories

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:54.270
and the lessons and the metaphors

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:55.860
and you can take a lot from it.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:58.190
And the biggest thing that
you take from it is that

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:02.040
it is proof that Joseph Smith
was actually called of God

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.320
to prepare the world
for the second coming,

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:05.970
that he was a legitimate prophet.

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:11.940
So Joseph Smith by 1830
has the Book of Mormon.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:13.620
He has proof that he's a prophet

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.700
and he starts to gain followers,
followers that believe him.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.660
And a group of those followers
get together in April of 1830

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.420
in a little house in Fayette, New York,

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.250
and they start a church.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.410
At this point, Joseph Smith is behaving

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.210
like a full-blown prophet.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.870
He says he's getting almost
daily communication from Jesus

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.060
and he starts to develop a theology

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:39.345
that is unlike anything else on offer.

00:16:39.345 --> 00:16:41.580
(light piano music)

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:45.900
Turns out that God is actually
a man with a body of flesh

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.033
and bone and he has a wife.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:53.460
God lives near a star that's far away.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:56.700
And we, all of us here on
earth, are these little

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.520
eternal balls of light
called intelligences,

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.430
but are heavenly parents have birthed us

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.350
into spiritual children.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.690
And then they sent us down onto this earth

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.970
to get a physical body, to get married,

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:12.900
to create an earthly family,
to learn and to grow.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.530
So that someday we can
return to live with God,

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.360
with our families,

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:23.250
and then we can become
like God with our spouses.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.470
We can create our own spiritual families

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:29.190
in some other part of the
universe, but in order to do that,

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:32.340
we have to pass some tests here on earth.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.990
We have to complete certain rituals

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.210
and demonstrate obedience to him.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:38.430
And in order to make this all happen,

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:40.347
he needs to set up a church.

00:17:40.347 --> 00:17:42.810
The church needs to have proper authority

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.670
and there would need to be a savior

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.700
that would come down to
account for all of our sins

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:51.630
so that we can be pure to enter
the Kingdom of God, again.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:55.470
Luckily, one of our spiritual
brothers named Jehovah later

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:59.223
called Jesus volunteered
to be this savior.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.400
Okay, but there's a big problem,

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.340
which is that God's children
are super rebellious.

00:18:05.340 --> 00:18:07.710
So over the years, God calls prophets

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.380
to organize his church
with the proper authority

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:12.660
and to do all of these special rituals

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.280
to teach them about Jesus.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.490
And eventually that truth
gets eroded and it fades away

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:20.820
and the world falls into
apostasy until it's ready again.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:23.880
When God calls another prophet
to restore his authority

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.530
and start the whole process over again,

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.300
this happens over and over.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:31.410
Until eventually Jesus came,
he was like the sixth prophet.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:34.470
He establishes his church
causes prophets and apostles

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:37.290
gives them the authority by
putting his hands on their head.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.720
And then of course he suffers for our sins

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.770
and dies on the cross.

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:43.560
But just like has happened over and over,

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.750
Jesus' church got corrupted,

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:48.300
it got mixed with power and politics

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.700
and the world fell back into the apostasy.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.860
This one's called the great apostasy.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:56.010
But eventually the world
would be coming to an end.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.480
Jesus would be coming soon

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.550
and things were about to get really bad.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:03.060
So God helped Europeans
come across the ocean

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.680
to take over North America,

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:06.960
colonize the land, and create a country

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:08.700
that had freedom of religion.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.470
Also, that a few decades later,

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:12.150
Joseph Smith could be born

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.880
and then called to restore his church.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.740
And that's how we get to the first vision.

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:20.130
Jesus and heavenly Father
appearing to Joseph Smith

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.440
in a grove, sending angels
to him to tell him where

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.820
to get the golden plates.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.220
And to solve for the
whole authority thing,

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.050
Joseph says that the apostles,

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.540
the original apostles of
Jesus Christ came to him

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.690
to restore the authority that priesthood

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.280
that Jesus had given them.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.900
So now he could establish his church.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:38.220
There was a restoration,

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.520
Joseph was the prophet of
a newly restored church

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.290
that he could talk to God,

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:46.500
he could get instruction on
exactly how to run God's Kingdom

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.200
here on earth to prepare the
world for the millennium.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.210
Okay, that was a lot.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.210
And lemme just say that was
a very summarized version

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:58.560
of LDS theology.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:02.010
Someday I'd like to make
a video about the details

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.430
because it's actually super
complex and super wild.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.600
The point I'm trying to make here is

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.870
that Joseph Smith's church
did indeed have a lot

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.870
of the ingredients of the
religious movements of the time,

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:16.560
last days, apocalypse preparing
God's Kingdom on the earth,

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:18.060
preparing for the millennium.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:20.160
This was all trending at the time.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:21.420
This was not surprising.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.630
But a lot of this stuff was totally new,

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.340
wild fringe doctrine.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:28.440
God has a body and a wife.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:33.150
This was a completely wild
blend of Jewish mysticism,

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.740
American folk magic,

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:38.040
reincarnation, evangelical Christianity.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:41.100
And eventually he even woven freemasonry.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.960
A totally fresh thing.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.520
There was nothing quite like it.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:48.870
It was super unique and super
potent and super polarizing.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.760
You either believed that Joseph Smith

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:53.820
was an incredibly inspired
prophet who was like revealing

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.950
the truth that none of
us had ever heard before,

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.560
or he was just a brilliant,
creative visionary

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.500
inventing this elaborate
plan to dupe people,

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.750
which is what a lot of
people in his village

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.360
started to think as he
started to gain followers.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.870
They had him arrested, calling
him a disorderly person.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.120
He eventually gets
released and he realizes

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:15.198
that he and his few members need to leave.

00:21:15.198 --> 00:21:18.270
(organ music)

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.050
This begins the long journey
of the Mormons moving west.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.640
Joseph and his followers set out.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.460
He's now talking to God
directly all of the time,

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:29.490
and he says that the Lord
is telling him to go to Ohio

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:33.210
to await instructions for
their actual final destination,

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:36.150
the place that they're actually
gonna set up their new city,

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.740
their millennial kingdom,

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:41.340
this communal utopian society
that would be the base

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:44.760
for preparing the world for
the second coming of Jesus.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.923
They would call it Zion.

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.150
And this is the most important part of

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:53.580
the entire story, Zion.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.560
If you want to understand Joseph Smith,

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.910
and if you want to understand the rest

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:58.230
of the Latter-day Saints movement,

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:01.743
including modern Mormonism,
you have to understand Zion.

00:22:02.856 --> 00:22:05.939
(suspenseful music)

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:10.170
Joseph says that the Lord is telling him

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:13.497
that he will give him the
exact location of Zion,

00:22:13.497 --> 00:22:16.230
and he tells him that it
will be quote "On the borders

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:17.520
by the Lamanites".

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.520
Remember that the Lamanites
are the American Indians.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:22.770
And so this actually works perfectly

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:25.590
because at this time, the U.S. government

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:28.620
is ethnically cleansing North America

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:31.110
and pushing first Americans west.

00:22:31.110 --> 00:22:33.810
So there's a lot of territory
where white settlers

00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:36.720
are budding up against Native Americans.

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:38.520
Zion's gonna be somewhere around here.

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:40.920
So Joseph and his
followers are now in Ohio

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:42.360
and they are growing.

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.010
People love this story.

00:22:44.010 --> 00:22:47.250
And the concept of Zion transitions
from this sort of vague,

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:51.330
idealistic idea to a very solid plan.

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:54.300
A new society called the new Jerusalem,

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:56.880
the new Jerusalem from
the prophecies of old.

00:22:56.880 --> 00:22:58.890
And it literally became a plan,

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:01.413
like he actually starts
to sketch it on paper.

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:07.080
We got these digital scans

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:10.428
of Joseph Smith's sketches of Zion.

00:23:10.428 --> 00:23:12.750
(light piano music)

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:15.381
He writes in extreme detail on exactly

00:23:15.381 --> 00:23:17.400
what this city will be.

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:20.310
This whole thing was based
on these gridded streets,

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.840
on perfectly parceled plots,

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:24.060
on no more than one square mile of land.

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:27.030
Joseph writes that "The
home should be 25 feet

00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:31.230
from the street to leave room
for a yard and plant gardens.

00:23:31.230 --> 00:23:34.080
All the houses were to be
brick or brick and stone,

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.510
and there should be farms
all around this city

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:37.650
that aren't too far."

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:40.710
The central streets of this
city nod to Joseph's love

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:43.320
for Jewish history and culture.

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:47.190
Zion Street, Jerusalem
Street, Bethlehem Street,

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.500
with the temple in the center of the city.

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:51.870
Spoiler alert, this is how Salt Lake City

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:54.750
and a lot of cities in
Utah are actually designed.

00:23:54.750 --> 00:23:56.040
But that's for part two.

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.920
I mean, what this shows is that
Joseph was taking this idea

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:02.790
of God's restored kingdom on
earth, totally, literally.

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:04.890
And it was gonna be hyper progressive,

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:07.260
a new communal society
where everyone would share

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:09.180
with one another, the
resources would be shared,

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:11.520
and the whole thing would be
governed by celestial laws

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:13.050
and governmental structures.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:15.360
A new government run by
the prophet where God

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:16.500
could talk to his people

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:19.320
while he prepared the world for its end.

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:22.260
Zion was a vision that
Joseph was uniquely good

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:23.640
at rallying around.

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:27.300
Charismatic and creative
leader, prolific and inspiring.

00:24:27.300 --> 00:24:29.790
His followers became deeply dedicated

00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:32.280
to this mission of establishing Zion,

00:24:32.280 --> 00:24:35.880
and it becomes the main
calling card for new converts.

00:24:35.880 --> 00:24:39.180
Joseph Smith's Millennial
Kingdom is the place to be

00:24:39.180 --> 00:24:40.110
when the world ends,

00:24:40.110 --> 00:24:41.860
and the world's ending any day now.

00:24:43.119 --> 00:24:46.290
(light upbeat music)

00:24:46.290 --> 00:24:47.880
So the church is growing in Ohio.

00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:49.770
They still don't know where
the final location of Zion

00:24:49.770 --> 00:24:52.560
is gonna be, and meanwhile,
Joseph is getting more and more

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:54.780
and more of these revelations,

00:24:54.780 --> 00:24:56.970
and he's pushing the
belief system of Mormonism

00:24:56.970 --> 00:24:59.370
further and further from
mainstream Christianity.

00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:00.690
Joseph comes out and says there actually

00:25:00.690 --> 00:25:02.070
is no heaven and hell,

00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:04.740
but rather there are
three kingdoms of heaven.

00:25:04.740 --> 00:25:07.440
All of us will be sorted
into these different kingdoms

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:10.440
depending on how obedient
we were here on earth,

00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:13.950
how much we accepted Christ
and repented of our sins.

00:25:13.950 --> 00:25:16.170
There's even a spiritual
prison and paradise

00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:17.460
that you go to after you die,

00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:19.830
but before you're sorted
into the kingdoms.

00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:21.690
In order to get to the
highest degree of kingdom,

00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:22.860
the celestial kingdom,

00:25:22.860 --> 00:25:25.590
you have to be married
by the proper authority

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:28.999
that will seal you to you and
your family forever and soon.

00:25:28.999 --> 00:25:31.740
Joseph says that more
angels are appearing to him

00:25:31.740 --> 00:25:34.920
to give him the authority
to do this sealing thing.

00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:38.403
Family is becoming core
to Mormon theology.

00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:42.453
But the good times don't last.

00:25:43.290 --> 00:25:47.070
The locals in Ohio and
their government don't love

00:25:47.070 --> 00:25:49.830
this vision of a new religious society.

00:25:49.830 --> 00:25:52.770
The flocks of new members
of the church arriving

00:25:52.770 --> 00:25:55.590
to this super well-organized, efficient,

00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:59.070
unified group of people led
by this charismatic prophet

00:25:59.070 --> 00:26:01.740
who has more and more fringe beliefs.

00:26:01.740 --> 00:26:04.110
One night Joseph is violently dragged

00:26:04.110 --> 00:26:06.420
from his home by a mob.

00:26:06.420 --> 00:26:09.150
He's covered in tar and feathers.

00:26:09.150 --> 00:26:11.790
They're telling him to leave and he does.

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:14.400
Luckily, one of Joseph's missionaries

00:26:14.400 --> 00:26:17.460
and former scribes Oliver
Cowdery had been out scouting

00:26:17.460 --> 00:26:18.360
where Zion should be,

00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:20.250
where the millennial
kingdom should be set up.

00:26:20.250 --> 00:26:22.830
And he comes back and
says he found the place,

00:26:22.830 --> 00:26:26.400
Jackson County, Missouri, 800 miles away.

00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:29.010
Indeed and just as the Lord said,

00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:31.987
right on the border with the Laymanites.

00:26:31.987 --> 00:26:35.310
"This would be Zion",
the Lord tells Joseph,

00:26:35.310 --> 00:26:36.870
the place where he is appointed

00:26:36.870 --> 00:26:38.970
for the gathering of the saints.

00:26:38.970 --> 00:26:41.460
And now there's a revelation
from the Lord saying

00:26:41.460 --> 00:26:43.620
that all of this land in Independence,

00:26:43.620 --> 00:26:46.560
Missouri should be
purchased by the saints.

00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:47.910
Buy up as much land as you can.

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:49.020
This is Zion.

00:26:49.020 --> 00:26:53.010
Oh, and it is revealed
to Joseph that this area,

00:26:53.010 --> 00:26:55.200
Independence, Missouri,
Jackson County, Missouri,

00:26:55.200 --> 00:26:58.440
is right next to the
original Garden of Eden

00:26:58.440 --> 00:27:00.750
like where Adam and Eve
like the first people were.

00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:04.050
It turns out that Missouri
is like the holy land,

00:27:04.050 --> 00:27:05.910
the epicenter for the end of the world,

00:27:05.910 --> 00:27:08.463
and the Garden of Eden is in Missouri.

00:27:10.320 --> 00:27:11.700
So Mormons start buying up land

00:27:11.700 --> 00:27:13.590
and they start moving to Missouri.

00:27:13.590 --> 00:27:14.550
And they did this quickly.

00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:15.600
This wasn't theoretical.

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:18.690
They thought that the second
coming was like weeks or months

00:27:18.690 --> 00:27:20.100
or just maybe a few years away.

00:27:20.100 --> 00:27:22.080
Martin Harris, one of the early converts,

00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:24.210
asserted that quote, "In four years,

00:27:24.210 --> 00:27:27.150
every religion in the
U.S. would be broken down

00:27:27.150 --> 00:27:29.400
and all would become Mormon,

00:27:29.400 --> 00:27:32.550
and that the rest of the
human race would just perish."

00:27:32.550 --> 00:27:33.960
And then he was so confident that he said

00:27:33.960 --> 00:27:36.660
that "If it didn't happen, he
would cut off his own hands."

00:27:36.660 --> 00:27:38.610
I mean, they were serious

00:27:38.610 --> 00:27:41.220
about building Zion in Missouri and quick.

00:27:41.220 --> 00:27:43.170
Okay, but not so fast.

00:27:43.170 --> 00:27:45.930
The locals like are not into this.

00:27:45.930 --> 00:27:50.730
They hear about this swarm of
Mormons coming to their county

00:27:50.730 --> 00:27:53.820
who want to turn their
city into a new religious,

00:27:53.820 --> 00:27:57.120
communal society and
prepare for the apocalypse.

00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:59.220
And now they're arriving by the thousands,

00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:02.490
which means they will have
more political power soon.

00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:04.980
They start to get scared
that the Mormons are plotting

00:28:04.980 --> 00:28:08.070
a takeover of their private
property all in the name

00:28:08.070 --> 00:28:10.500
of building Zion, and they're
not gonna stand for it.

00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:12.240
They want the Mormons out.

00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:14.940
So they start sabotaging
them with violence,

00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:17.850
vandalizing their stores,
destroying their homes,

00:28:17.850 --> 00:28:19.590
assaulting Mormon leaders.

00:28:19.590 --> 00:28:21.360
It gets really violent.

00:28:21.360 --> 00:28:25.050
And at first, Joseph tells his
followers to not fight back.

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:27.783
And once again, the
Mormons are driven out.

00:28:29.490 --> 00:28:32.850
The next five years are
years of conflict for Joseph

00:28:32.850 --> 00:28:34.560
and his growing church.

00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:37.110
They're on the move all over the Midwest,

00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:39.330
at each stop facing violent resistance

00:28:39.330 --> 00:28:41.670
from local residents and
government officials.

00:28:41.670 --> 00:28:44.490
So Joseph and his followers
are done being passive.

00:28:44.490 --> 00:28:46.770
They start fighting back and it escalates

00:28:46.770 --> 00:28:48.840
into basically a full blown war.

00:28:48.840 --> 00:28:50.670
The governor of Missouri issues

00:28:50.670 --> 00:28:53.287
a literal extermination
order saying quote,

00:28:53.287 --> 00:28:55.950
"The Mormons must be treated as enemies

00:28:55.950 --> 00:28:57.960
and must be exterminated or driven

00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:00.930
from the state if necessary
for public peace."

00:29:00.930 --> 00:29:02.310
It's getting really bad.

00:29:02.310 --> 00:29:06.000
So they flee once more to
Illinois where the government,

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:09.690
who includes a young lawmaker
named Abraham Lincoln,

00:29:09.690 --> 00:29:13.350
gives them a special
charter to create a city

00:29:13.350 --> 00:29:14.820
and a government that is fit

00:29:14.820 --> 00:29:17.250
for their unique Zion principles.

00:29:17.250 --> 00:29:19.110
They call this city Nauvoo,

00:29:19.110 --> 00:29:21.868
Hebrew for beautiful or beautiful place.

00:29:21.868 --> 00:29:24.368
(calm music)

00:29:25.350 --> 00:29:28.860
Okay, so even though the Lord
had said to Joseph that he had

00:29:28.860 --> 00:29:31.650
prepared Missouri to
be the place for Zion,

00:29:31.650 --> 00:29:34.920
the Saints were gonna have to
settle for Illinois for now,

00:29:34.920 --> 00:29:37.650
and they feel safe
protected by this charter

00:29:37.650 --> 00:29:39.600
and they start creating Zion.

00:29:39.600 --> 00:29:41.670
There's a total merger
between church and state,

00:29:41.670 --> 00:29:43.740
a complete religiously run settlement

00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:46.830
where Joseph appoints himself
to be in charge of the courts

00:29:46.830 --> 00:29:49.380
as well as the newly strengthened militia.

00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:52.020
They now have a full army
to protect themselves.

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:54.750
Joseph had been sending
missionaries to Europe to preach

00:29:54.750 --> 00:29:56.340
about the gospel and invite people

00:29:56.340 --> 00:29:58.680
to come join his vision of Zion.

00:29:58.680 --> 00:30:01.770
And one of those people is my
like great-great-grandfather

00:30:01.770 --> 00:30:04.440
who was converted by a
missionary in England

00:30:04.440 --> 00:30:07.980
and then traveled to the
United States with his family

00:30:07.980 --> 00:30:11.400
and pregnant wife in
pursuit of finding Zion.

00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:14.790
And they arrived to Nauvoo,
a city that eventually grew

00:30:14.790 --> 00:30:17.430
to be more populous than Chicago.

00:30:17.430 --> 00:30:19.590
And it's in Nauvoo where Joseph says

00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:22.830
that an angel appeared to him
and demanded, multiple times,

00:30:22.830 --> 00:30:26.550
against his will, that he
take on multiple wives,

00:30:26.550 --> 00:30:28.380
that those wives are sealed to him.

00:30:28.380 --> 00:30:30.870
His first plural marriage is to a teenager

00:30:30.870 --> 00:30:34.080
and he goes on to have 40
wives in just three years.

00:30:34.080 --> 00:30:36.480
Many of them were married to other people,

00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:39.210
but then were sealed
to Joseph the prophet.

00:30:39.210 --> 00:30:41.850
What I find striking here
is that up until this point,

00:30:41.850 --> 00:30:45.810
you have this meticulous
documentation of every single

00:30:45.810 --> 00:30:50.490
revelation and theology rule
and new policy in the church

00:30:50.490 --> 00:30:52.680
here in what's called
the doctrine covenants.

00:30:52.680 --> 00:30:56.040
But polygamy stayed quiet and private.

00:30:56.040 --> 00:30:59.340
It was one of those revelations
reserved for just Joseph

00:30:59.340 --> 00:31:01.053
and the leaders that he chose.

00:31:02.610 --> 00:31:07.610
By 1844, the Zion dream
is actually catching fire.

00:31:07.860 --> 00:31:09.660
It's growing in Illinois,

00:31:09.660 --> 00:31:13.110
and Joseph decides to run for president.

00:31:13.110 --> 00:31:15.060
Now, he didn't have a
big chance of winning,

00:31:15.060 --> 00:31:17.640
but in his mind and the
mind of his followers,

00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:19.530
this was the natural next step.

00:31:19.530 --> 00:31:20.670
They were establishing Zion,

00:31:20.670 --> 00:31:23.730
and Zion was going to be
the new society on earth.

00:31:23.730 --> 00:31:26.970
But this presidential
campaign miserably backfires

00:31:26.970 --> 00:31:30.720
because now he has seen as a
legitimate political threat.

00:31:30.720 --> 00:31:33.480
He's too good at gaining new followers.

00:31:33.480 --> 00:31:36.660
It gets worse when one group
of former Latter-day Saints,

00:31:36.660 --> 00:31:38.940
who didn't agree with Joseph decide

00:31:38.940 --> 00:31:42.480
to publish a newspaper in
Nauvoo that criticized him

00:31:42.480 --> 00:31:45.630
for polygamy and generally his leadership.

00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:47.340
Joseph has done messing
around at this point.

00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:48.750
He's become very militant,

00:31:48.750 --> 00:31:50.610
and he responds by sending his militia

00:31:50.610 --> 00:31:52.740
to destroy their printing press.

00:31:52.740 --> 00:31:55.620
He declares martial law, and
now the government of Illinois

00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:57.720
who had given them this
sort of safe charter,

00:31:57.720 --> 00:32:00.150
sees this chaos and they're not into it.

00:32:00.150 --> 00:32:03.390
And they arrest Joseph for
attempting to incite a riot.

00:32:03.390 --> 00:32:05.430
Now, this was one of
many run-ins with the law

00:32:05.430 --> 00:32:07.080
that Joseph Smith had didn't cover them.

00:32:07.080 --> 00:32:08.220
Some of them were legitimate,

00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:09.390
some of them were trumped up,

00:32:09.390 --> 00:32:12.030
but now he's caused a real disruption.

00:32:12.030 --> 00:32:14.580
He gets locked up in
jail and two days later,

00:32:14.580 --> 00:32:18.390
a mob of more than 200
men storm this jail.

00:32:18.390 --> 00:32:20.340
They climb up to the
second floor where Joseph

00:32:20.340 --> 00:32:22.590
and his brother are,
and they shoot at him.

00:32:22.590 --> 00:32:26.373
He tries to jump out the window
and he falls to his death.

00:32:27.870 --> 00:32:32.010
The prophet is dead at 38.
(gun shots)

00:32:32.010 --> 00:32:34.020
Joseph Smith is now a martyr.

00:32:34.020 --> 00:32:36.780
He died with a Book of
Mormon in his hands,

00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:40.713
defending his vision, his
belief in his own story.

00:32:42.390 --> 00:32:46.230
This poured fuel on the
fire of his vision for Zion.

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:48.330
But the Latter-day Saints start to realize

00:32:48.330 --> 00:32:49.530
that if they're gonna build Zion,

00:32:49.530 --> 00:32:52.080
it's not gonna be in the United States.

00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:54.000
They need to look further afoot.

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.490
They need a place far
away where they can build

00:32:56.490 --> 00:32:59.310
their millennial kingdom
without being harassed for it.

00:32:59.310 --> 00:33:02.190
So you look far to the west, to Mexico,

00:33:02.190 --> 00:33:05.850
and the next chapter of the
story is the move into Mexico

00:33:05.850 --> 00:33:08.310
and the establishment of their Zion

00:33:08.310 --> 00:33:11.610
next to a large salty
lake in the high desert.

00:33:11.610 --> 00:33:14.490
And that is a story I'll
tell you in part two.

00:33:14.490 --> 00:33:16.860
But for now, I want to just tell you

00:33:16.860 --> 00:33:20.040
my thoughts on Joseph Smith.

00:33:20.040 --> 00:33:23.730
As someone who spent most of
my life believing this story,

00:33:23.730 --> 00:33:26.370
basing my life and my worldview around it,

00:33:26.370 --> 00:33:28.830
doing this story and looking
at it from an objective

00:33:28.830 --> 00:33:31.623
historical lens has taught me a lot.

00:33:32.790 --> 00:33:35.700
Joseph Smith created
something really powerful.

00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:37.200
You can't deny that.

00:33:37.200 --> 00:33:39.570
It was a story about the last days.

00:33:39.570 --> 00:33:43.410
It was a story full of
treasure and visions and angels

00:33:43.410 --> 00:33:45.690
and modern day revelation from God.

00:33:45.690 --> 00:33:48.630
It was a story about a chosen people,

00:33:48.630 --> 00:33:51.240
a utopian society of one heart

00:33:51.240 --> 00:33:54.990
and one mind, safety, enlightenment.

00:33:54.990 --> 00:33:56.850
There's a reason why every year,

00:33:56.850 --> 00:34:00.210
Latter-day Saints go back to
that hill in upstate New York

00:34:00.210 --> 00:34:02.160
where Joseph said he found the plates

00:34:02.160 --> 00:34:05.880
and they put on this
insanely ambitious production

00:34:05.880 --> 00:34:08.850
on a stage that's like 10 levels deep

00:34:08.850 --> 00:34:11.790
with almost a thousand
characters where they reenact

00:34:11.790 --> 00:34:14.310
the story of Joseph Smith, their prophet.

00:34:14.310 --> 00:34:17.400
They reenact him finding the
plates, translating them,

00:34:17.400 --> 00:34:19.770
and then they act out the
story of the Book of Mormon.

00:34:19.770 --> 00:34:22.357
There's a reason why Latter-day
Saints sing a song called,

00:34:22.357 --> 00:34:25.290
"Praise to the Man", where
they laud Joseph Smith,

00:34:25.290 --> 00:34:28.110
the prophet who opened
the last dispensation,

00:34:28.110 --> 00:34:30.232
who restored the truth to the world.

00:34:30.232 --> 00:34:32.520
♪ Jesus anointed the prophet ♪

00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:33.840
I believed this.

00:34:33.840 --> 00:34:36.060
I believed this well into my twenties.

00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:37.680
I found deep comfort in it.

00:34:37.680 --> 00:34:41.010
I found community in
being a part of a religion

00:34:41.010 --> 00:34:43.380
that was so different
than every other religion,

00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:45.990
and that was very often mocked for it.

00:34:45.990 --> 00:34:48.570
The martyrdom and the
persecution of Joseph

00:34:48.570 --> 00:34:53.250
and his followers became
proof that this was true

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:55.680
and that it was being
persecuted in these last days,

00:34:55.680 --> 00:34:58.890
just like the prophecies
in the Bible told us about.

00:34:58.890 --> 00:35:02.250
And I was compelled by
this idea of the last days.

00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:05.550
The problem with getting
caught up in the beauty

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:10.110
and the comfort, and the
narrative of being a chosen people

00:35:10.110 --> 00:35:14.430
in the last days is that
it allows you to ignore.

00:35:14.430 --> 00:35:16.440
I think that's what a lot
of people have done over

00:35:16.440 --> 00:35:18.870
the decades with Joseph's story.

00:35:18.870 --> 00:35:20.970
They ignore, they ignore something

00:35:20.970 --> 00:35:23.640
that I guess is plain for me to see now,

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:24.940
on the other side of this.

00:35:29.235 --> 00:35:32.220
(light piano music)

00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:35.433
Brother, I am happy, happy man.

00:35:37.506 --> 00:35:38.339
I've been for more than a missionary

00:35:38.339 --> 00:35:40.239
for more than a year now, I can relax.

00:35:41.370 --> 00:35:43.860
Joseph Smith was a charismatic
leader who knew how

00:35:43.860 --> 00:35:46.800
to tell stories about
magic, about visions,

00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:48.060
and about treasure.

00:35:48.060 --> 00:35:50.400
He had known how to do that
since he was a teenager.

00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:53.130
Well before he decided he was
going to become a prophet.

00:35:53.130 --> 00:35:55.440
He found an audience in doing this.

00:35:55.440 --> 00:35:58.980
He attracted people to him
with his visionary skills,

00:35:58.980 --> 00:36:03.540
and he used those skills to
invent a complex set of stories

00:36:03.540 --> 00:36:06.600
about Native Americans
actually being Israelites,

00:36:06.600 --> 00:36:09.570
about heavenly parents,
preparing the world for its end

00:36:09.570 --> 00:36:10.950
and about the priesthood,

00:36:10.950 --> 00:36:15.570
this authority that we all
must participate in to receive

00:36:15.570 --> 00:36:17.490
the rituals and ordinances

00:36:17.490 --> 00:36:20.100
that only one church can administer.

00:36:20.100 --> 00:36:23.250
And eventually, he used these
stories to build a movement

00:36:23.250 --> 00:36:27.180
around his vision that
allowed him to take 40 wives

00:36:27.180 --> 00:36:31.500
and build an army and break
laws and bully his enemies.

00:36:31.500 --> 00:36:33.720
When you are a Latter-day Saint,

00:36:33.720 --> 00:36:35.310
these facts are written off

00:36:35.310 --> 00:36:38.790
as anti-Mormon literature or persecution.

00:36:38.790 --> 00:36:42.390
But for me, having left
the church and spent years

00:36:42.390 --> 00:36:46.140
rewiring my brain and my
programming of these stories,

00:36:46.140 --> 00:36:47.760
I see them as facts.

00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:50.610
And frankly, they're not that surprising.

00:36:50.610 --> 00:36:54.420
This is the same old story of
a charismatic, visionary man

00:36:54.420 --> 00:36:57.510
who tells a story of apocalyptic endings

00:36:57.510 --> 00:37:00.120
to gain followers, to gain power,

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:02.760
and then decides that he
deserves a lot of women,

00:37:02.760 --> 00:37:04.680
and then he dies for the cause,

00:37:04.680 --> 00:37:07.950
leaving a movement that
continues his vision.

00:37:07.950 --> 00:37:10.710
Oftentimes those movements
get more and more dogmatic.

00:37:10.710 --> 00:37:14.490
They use shame to keep
their people close to them,

00:37:14.490 --> 00:37:18.480
and they revere their prophet long after

00:37:18.480 --> 00:37:19.650
that prophet is dead.

00:37:19.650 --> 00:37:22.530
And yet, what's complicated
about this is I can't help,

00:37:22.530 --> 00:37:26.490
but feel a deep sense of sadness
for having lost my belief

00:37:26.490 --> 00:37:27.543
in Joseph's story.

00:37:28.794 --> 00:37:29.970
I can't explain it,

00:37:29.970 --> 00:37:32.520
but these stories are
incredibly comforting

00:37:32.520 --> 00:37:35.640
when you believe in
them, they're motivating.

00:37:35.640 --> 00:37:38.800
These creative stories unlike
any other belief system

00:37:39.870 --> 00:37:41.250
can be really beautiful.

00:37:41.250 --> 00:37:45.900
And that is a paradox that
there's really no resolution for.

00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:46.980
There's a lot more to say on this,

00:37:46.980 --> 00:37:50.100
but I'm gonna save it for
part two on the series

00:37:50.100 --> 00:37:53.550
where we see what happens
next after Joseph is murdered

00:37:53.550 --> 00:37:55.800
and the Latter-day Saints move west

00:37:55.800 --> 00:38:00.363
to find their vision of Zion, okay.

00:38:01.864 --> 00:38:04.950
(birds chirping)

00:38:04.950 --> 00:38:07.950
(light calm music)

00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:22.950
Okay, well, thanks for watching.

00:38:22.950 --> 00:38:24.270
And if you're still here,

00:38:24.270 --> 00:38:27.540
I know that was a bit of
a emotional rollercoaster

00:38:27.540 --> 00:38:28.373
there at the end,

00:38:28.373 --> 00:38:30.960
especially if you are
someone who was associated

00:38:30.960 --> 00:38:32.070
with the church in any way.

00:38:32.070 --> 00:38:33.720
And there's a lot there.

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:36.030
And I know in making this video,

00:38:36.030 --> 00:38:39.270
I felt a lot of feelings and
rehashed a lot of things,

00:38:39.270 --> 00:38:40.410
but I think doing it,

00:38:40.410 --> 00:38:43.110
telling this story has been
pretty cathartic for me,

00:38:43.110 --> 00:38:44.790
and I'm really looking
forward to the discussion

00:38:44.790 --> 00:38:47.970
in the comments about what
others feel about this stuff.

00:38:47.970 --> 00:38:49.110
Let me tell you about a couple things.

